<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged by the Tauri CLI into the iOS app's Info.plist (it looks for Info.ios.plist next to
  tauri.conf.json). iOS readiness, 2026-11-12.

  - NSCameraUsageDescription: REQUIRED. The QR scanner uses the camera through the webview
    (getUserMedia); without this string iOS ends the app the first time the camera is asked for,
    and App Review rejects a camera app without one. English only for now; translations go in
    the Xcode project's InfoPlist.strings once `tauri ios init` has made it.
  - CFBundleDisplayName: the name under the home-screen icon. "SignBit", the same as the Android
    launcher label (gen/android strings.xml app_name), since "SignBit Fountain" is cut off
    there; the icon and the App Store page carry the rest (confirmed by the founder, 2026-11-12).
  - ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption = NO: the founder's answer to App Store Connect's export
    compliance question (2026-11-12: "id say no ... its the users that are encrypting their own
    data"). Fountain's encryption only protects the user's own keys and backup on their device
    with their own passphrase, and its signatures are signatures; it sends nothing. Set here so
    every upload stops asking. Revisit only if Fountain ever encrypts data it SENDS.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Fountain uses the camera only to scan QR codes, such as a payment to sign. Nothing it sees is saved or sent anywhere.</string>
  <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
  <string>SignBit</string>
  <key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
